## Self-Review: Spec Coverage Check

| Spec requirement | Covered by |
|---|---|
| Add Pano section to Add/Edit Information modal | Task 3 |
| One Information record stores at most one pano | Task 2 data shape and Task 3 single input |
| Area Information shows at most one pano action in preview | Task 5 |
| Validate TourMkr URLs with tour id and pano id | Task 1 and Task 3 |
| Preserve optional heading/tilt values | Task 1 parser and tests |
| Render pano in full overlay modal iframe | Task 4 and Task 5 |
| No multiple panos / no project import / no API fetch / no auth | Global Constraints and file map |
| Reference only; no pano image copy | Global Constraints and Task 3 input-only flow |
| Point and Safety do not show pano action | Task 5 visibility and manual QA |
| Store and persistence preserve pano | Task 2 and Task 6 manual refresh/export checks |
| Unit tests for parser | Task 1 |
| Component/manual verification for modal open/close | Task 5 and Task 6 |
| Accessibility: button, dialog, close label, Escape, iframe title | Task 4 |
| Fallback external link if iframe fails/blocks | Task 4 |

## Execution Notes

- The existing repository may have unrelated baseline blockers:
  - `tsc`/build can fail on missing `@/auth` in `src/actions/billing.ts`.
  - full Vitest can fail if `samples/sample2-txt/a.txt` is absent.
  - full ESLint can fail on auth page lint issues.
- Do not fix those in this feature unless the user explicitly asks. Use focused checks to verify this work and record baseline blockers separately.
- TourMkr iframe behavior is an integration risk. If the normal share URL is blocked by `X-Frame-Options` or CSP `frame-ancestors`, keep the modal and external fallback, then coordinate a TourMkr embed URL contract as a follow-up.
